--
std::map operator[] insertion, verifying in ~1.4s.  Fixed by a chain of
front-end conformance fixes to the piecewise-construction machinery
(see the sibling minimal tests):
* [temp.deduct.type]/8 pack form mismatch rejects the candidate instead of
  resurrecting an empty pack (cpp11_pack_mismatch_not_empty: the
  swap<void> collateral);
* [expr.ref]/6 reference-member access is an lvalue +
  [over.best.ics.general]/2 non-viable candidates are not hard errors
  (cpp11_rvalue_ref_member_lvalue: _Head_base<I, T&&>/_Tuple_impl);
* [temp.variadic]/5 type-pack element substitution in declaration
  initializers (cpp11_pack_expansion_decl_init: _M_emplace_hint_unique's
  _Auto_node);
* [temp.deduct.type] primary-relative arguments for full-specialization
  instances (cpp11_pack_deduction_explicit_spec);
* [temp.param]/14 two independent packs in std::pair's piecewise
  constructor (cpp11_piecewise_ctor_two_packs);
* allocator_traits::construct model body gated to the single
  same-type-argument case, leaving piecewise construction to the real
  header body.
The earlier KNOWNBUG note attributed the failure to BMC scaling on the
inlined machinery; with the mis-instantiated code gone, the formula is
small.
